  "description": "Test build of Azir's Sun Disc, his Imperial Guards facing the charge and his sand soldiers from the side (needs League of Legends Heroes): replaces the main pack's Azir so that the Sun Disc rises from a fallen tower's ruin - his, or the enemy's outside their base - every 90 seconds (League's cooldown) and strikes the nearest enemy every second, the guards of Emperor's Divide face the way the wall charges, stand one by one in a single line across it and stand as a wall for 5 seconds, and his sand soldiers stand side-on facing the nearest enemy and thrust their spears when they strike, joined to him by a line of flowing sand while they stand within his reach (League's 660); a soldier he leaves out of that reach stops and crumbles, and one in an enemy tower's range ages twice as fast; Conquering Sands sends every soldier dashing to whatever enemy it targets, each dealing its damage and slow to the enemies on its path, and a soldier's stab goes through a line (League's) (the data pack cannot see the towers, the wall's direction, which side an enemy is on, nor draw a line between two moving points, nor tell Conquering Sands' target from the units round it). His skills are otherwise the main pack's. Other champions are untouched. Writes a log for testing.",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-17",
  "mod_id": "league_azir",
  "mod_type": "native",
  "name": "League Heroes: Azir's Sun Disc, charging guards and side-on soldiers (test)",
  "version": "0.3.0"
}
